-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions of seat deployer from part P0 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P0-cases-seat-deployer: the cases of the questions in P0-seat-deployer.l4: the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Regulation before the file was run and is written beside its assertion with the words that license it;
-- none was copied from the encoding's output. A failing assertion is a finding, never an expectation to edit.
-- Dates the cases stand on: 31 July 2024 (the day before entry into force), 1 August 2024, 1 and 2 February 2025 (Chapter I), 26 and 27 July 2026 (each side of the Omnibus),
-- 1 and 2 August 2026 (the general date), 2 December 2026, 2 August 2027, 2 December 2027, 2 August 2028, 2 August 2030, 31 December 2030, as each function needs.
-- A MIRROR comment marks a case whose facts are asked, with the same answer, in the case file of another seat (the Guide, section 3).
-- A #TRACE is preceded by its -- EXPECT line (FULFILLED, BREACH or OPEN: the obligation still pending). The clock of a trace is the number of days since the day the rule counts from.
-- Assertions: 175. Traces: 16.

§ `Article 1: does Chapter I apply on the date asked?`

-- Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked
-- 1 January 2024, before the Regulation exists: JUST FALSE, the Regulation has not entered into force (Art 113, first paragraph: "on the twentieth day following that of its publication")
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 31 July 2024, the day before entry into force: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 31 7 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 August 2024, in force but Chapter I applies only from 2 February 2025: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 February 2025, the day before Chapter I applies (Art 113(a)): JUST FALSE
-- MIRROR Art 113(a): whether Chapter I applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, the day Chapter I applies (Art 113(a)): JUST TRUE
-- MIRROR Art 113(a): whether Chapter I applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 2 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 26 July 2026, the text as enacted still in force: JUST TRUE (as enacted point (a): "Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST TRUE (point (a) as replaced keeps 2 February 2025 for Chapters I and II)
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE


§ `Article 2(1): does the Regulation apply to me?`

-- Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in the Union
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 1 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(b) answers (the deployer in the Union: a deployer in a third country is limb (c)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in the Union` (Date 1 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, a deployer established or located in the Union: JUST TRUE ("deployers of AI systems that have their place of establishment or are located within the Union")
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(b) answers (the deployer in the Union: a deployer in a third country is limb (c)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
-- MIRROR Art 2(1)(b) and (g): a deployer in the Union and a person affected by its AI system, located in the Union
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 February 2025, a deployer in a third country: NOTHING under limb (b); limb (c) is asked in its own question
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(b) answers (the deployer in the Union: a deployer in a third country is limb (c)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST TRUE (limb (b) was not changed)
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 27 7 2026) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(b) answers (the deployer in the Union: a deployer in a third country is limb (c)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in the Union` (Date 27 7 2026) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in a third country because the output of my AI system is used in the Union
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 1 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(c) answers (the provider or deployer in a third country whose output is used in the Union: one in the Union is limb (a) or (b)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in a third country because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 1 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, a party in a third country whose output is used in the Union: JUST TRUE ("where the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union")
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(c) answers (the provider or deployer in a third country whose output is used in the Union: one in the Union is limb (a) or (b)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
-- MIRROR Art 2(1)(c): a provider and a deployer in a third country whose AI system output is used in the Union
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in a third country because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 February 2025, a party in a third country whose output is not used in the Union: NOTHING (limited by "where the output ... is used in the Union")
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(c) answers (the provider or deployer in a third country whose output is used in the Union: one in the Union is limb (a) or (b)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in a third country because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, a party in the Union: NOTHING under limb (c), which speaks of a place in a third country (limbs (a) and (b) are asked in their own questions)
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(c) answers (the provider or deployer in a third country whose output is used in the Union: one in the Union is limb (a) or (b)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in a third country because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST TRUE (limb (c) was not changed)
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 27 7 2026) `Established or located in a third country` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(c) answers (the provider or deployer in a third country whose output is used in the Union: one in the Union is limb (a) or (b)); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in a third country because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` (Date 27 7 2026) `Established or located in a third country` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE


§ `Article 2(2): my high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (replaced by the Omnibus)`

-- Under Article 2(2), as a deployer of an AI system, does the provision I name apply to my high-risk AI system with Section B products
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(2), as a deployer of an AI system, does the provision I name apply to my high-risk AI system with Section B products` (Date 1 2 2025) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` TRUE FALSE 6 "" 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 26 July 2026 (text as enacted), Article 6(1) itself: JUST TRUE (as enacted: "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(2), as a deployer of an AI system, does the provision I name apply to my high-risk AI system with Section B products` (Date 26 7 2026) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` TRUE FALSE 6 "" 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 26 July 2026, the whole of Article 6: NOTHING, because only paragraph 1 of it is named and a reference to the whole Article is mixed
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(2), as a deployer of an AI system, does the provision I name apply to my high-risk AI system with Section B products` (Date 26 7 2026) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` TRUE FALSE 6 "" 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 26 July 2026, Article 9: JUST FALSE (as enacted: "only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply": Article 9 is not named)
-- MIRROR Art 2(2): the same Article asked from each operator seat about the same high-risk AI system
